* Wed Sep 02 2026 Hazel Caballero <hazel@sicura.us> - 3.0.0
- Reduce blast radius: a bare `include dconf` now only installs the package
  - `user_profile` is now `Optional` and defaults to `undef`; the default
    user/local/site/distro profile hierarchy was removed from data/common.yaml
    (the deep-merge lookup_options for `user_profile` are retained, so site
    Hiera values still merge across levels)
  - `tidy` now defaults to `false` (no purge of unmanaged files in managed
    profile directories unless explicitly enabled)
  - Deprecated the `use_user_profile_defaults` and `use_user_settings_defaults`
    parameters (setting them issues a deprecation warning); behavior is driven
    by `user_profile`/`user_settings` being set, though an explicit `false`
    still suppresses the corresponding resources
  - Removed the automatic `ensure => absent` cleanup of the default
    `dconf::settings` when `user_settings` was unset
- COORDINATION: simp/gnome, simp/mate, and simp/gdm relied on the removed
  default hierarchy contributing `user-db:user` to /etc/dconf/profile/user;
  they pin simp/dconf < 3.0.0 and must declare their own `user` database
  entry (or enforce simp:defaults) before widening their dependency range
- Add a `simp:defaults` compliance_engine profile that restores the pre-3.0.0
  defaults (activate with `compliance_engine::enforcement: [simp:defaults]`).
  Note the restored `dconf::tidy: true` only takes effect on directories
  managed by `dconf::settings` resources; the pre-3.0.0 cleanup resource that
  purged /etc/dconf/db/Defaults.d on a bare include is not restored
- `dconf::settings` now always falls back to
  `dconf::user_profile_defaults_name` when `profile` is not given (pre-3.0.0
  manifests that omitted `profile` keep compiling after the upgrade)
- `Dconf::DBSettings` now requires at least one database entry: an empty
  hash is a compile error instead of silently writing an empty profile file
  over the vendor-shipped one
- `dconf::settings` with `ensure => absent` now removes the settings file
  (previously it left an empty file behind)
- Drop the unused `simp/simp_options` dependency; declare the previously
  missing `puppetlabs/concat` and `puppetlabs/inifile` runtime dependencies;
  raise the `puppetlabs/stdlib` floor to 9.2.0 (3-argument `deprecation()`
  and `stdlib::ensure_packages`)
- Drop the never-functional `--` knockout_prefix from the
  `dconf::user_profile` lookup_options (knockout blanks a value, which
  `Dconf::DBSettings` rejects; the deep merge itself is unchanged)
- Document the on-disk layout the examples produce (fixes #67)

